.TH CONSIGNE 1 "2026-08-11" "realisateur" "deposit prose into the vault"
.SH NAME
consigne \- deposit prose into the Obsidian vault, and report what a deposit
left behind
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B consigne
.I path\fR...
.br
.B consigne status
.RI [ project ...]
.br
.B consigne
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B consigne
is the front door for the vault-consign step of
.IR PROSE-REAPING.md .
.PP
It is
.B not
a second implementation of
.BR "fonde consign" .
It runs the same mechanism \(em bibliothecaire's
.IR lib/consign-prose.sh ,
itself vendored from basheur's
.I impl/consign-prose
\(em located at runtime and never copied. There is one implementation and two
doors:
.BR "fonde consign" ,
the old one, which still works and says that it is old; and this one.
.PP
.B "consigne <path>..."
is therefore equivalent to
.B "fonde consign <path>..."
by construction rather than by promise: the same argv reaches the same
program with the same vault, so the deposit, the frontmatter, the read-back
gate, the overwrite refusal and the exit code are the same in both doors.
.SS status
.B consigne status
answers the question a deposit leaves open and nothing else asks:
.B what is in the vault AND still in the repo?
.PP
.IR consign-prose.sh " deletes nothing"
\(em it deposits, then reports what is now safe to remove. That is correct;
removal needs a judgement the depositor cannot make. But nothing consumed that
report, so the second half of every reaping pass existed only in the scrollback
of the terminal that ran the first half. hf7y/scheduler#86 measured the result
on 2026-08-10: 2,391 lines sitting in one repository and in the vault at once,
byte-for-byte, nine days after the deposit.
.PP
Each row is classified against the note's own recorded provenance \(em the
.IR source_repo ", " source_path " and " source_sha256
that the deposit itself wrote \(em not against a list:
.TP
.B DUPLICATED
the source file is still present and still byte-identical. The pass deposited
and stopped. This is the queue.
.TP
.B DIVERGED
still present, no longer the same bytes. Worse than DUPLICATED: the vault note
is a stale fork of a file somebody has since edited, and neither copy says so.
.TP
.B REAPED
the source file is gone. The pass finished.
.TP
.B UNREADABLE
the note carries no usable provenance, or its source repository is not on this
host. Named, never silently skipped.
.PP
A count and a prompt are printed after the rows.
.B It removes nothing.
Acting on the queue is the per-paragraph judgement
.I PROSE-REAPING.md
\(sc1 asks for, and there is deliberately no flag here that makes it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-summon
Accepted, and buys nothing. The deposit is mechanized and reaches no agent, so
this spends zero and says so on stderr \(em exactly as
.B "fonde consign \-\-summon"
does. That form is the remedy
.B fauche
prints for unconsigned prose, so it must not be a usage error here either.
Rejected on
.BR status ,
which never spends.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage text and exit 0.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BIBLIOTHECAIRE_VAULT
The vault. Default
.IR /srv/ecosystem1-vault ,
the FHS location for data a system serves; it was
.I $HOME/ecosystem1/ecosystem1
until 2026-08-12, which put the estate's prose in one user's home on one laptop.
This is the same variable and the same default
.BR fonde " and " fauche
read, deliberately: a caller who has pointed one door at another tree must
not have to learn a second name to point the others at the same place.
.B \-\-vault
overrides it for a single invocation.
.TP
.B CONSIGNE_IMPL
Path to
.IR lib/consign-prose.sh ,
when it should not be found automatically. Otherwise the resolution order is:
the installed
.BR fonde 's
own tree, then
.BR "installe list" 's
row for
.BR fonde ,
then a bibliothecaire checkout under
.BR $INSTALLE_PROJECTS .
Each candidate is probed, not assumed. If none answers, that is exit 6 and it
says so; it does not quietly deposit nothing.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Byte-identical to
.BR fonde 's
own contract, because on the deposit path it is literally the same process's
exit code, unwrapped.
.TP
.B 0
kept \(em deposited, or status read cleanly.
.TP
.B 2
usage \(em bad arguments, or a path that does not exist.
.TP
.B 5
broken \(em a note was written and read back with a different body.
.TP
.B 6
blind \(em could not read the vault, a source, or the mechanism itself.
.TP
.B 7
refused \(em would have overwritten an existing note, or the vault is not under
version control.
.SH NOTES
.B Never pushes, and never commits.
No code path runs
.B git push
or
.BR "git commit" .
It writes files and stops; the reaping pass that ran it commits and pushes
\(em
.I PROSE-REAPING.md
\(sc5.6. The private
.I hf7y/ecosystem1\-vault
remote IS the vault as of 2026-08-12, Zach-directed; the older
"deliberately left unpushed" rule is reversed, and what it cost is recorded in
.I PROSE-REAPING.md
\(sc2.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR fonde (1),
.BR fauche (1),
.I PROSE-REAPING.md
in hf7y/realisateur, hf7y/scheduler#86 for the half
.B status
makes countable, and
.I bin/tests/consigne.test.sh
for the suite that pins the two doors to one call shape.
